 "notes": "Base-game pack. Encounter pools generated from PokéAPI data, merged to location level across sub-areas, encounter methods, and the paired versions (in-game trades and raid/event distributions excluded); area order is estimated from encounter levels and is approximate. No encounter tables are available from PokéAPI for this game — use custom areas in the encounter log to track catches. Bosses ordered by levelCap ascending = recommended play order across the three story paths. Version variants: the Quaking Earth Titan is Great Tusk in Scarlet / Iron Treads in Violet (same level 45, Asado Desert). The final professor boss shown is AI Sada (Scarlet); in Violet, AI Turo uses Iron Moth 66, Iron Bundle 66, Iron Hands 66, Iron Jugulis 66, Iron Thorns 66, Iron Valiant 67. After Sada's team, a scripted second phase pits the player's Koraidon against her Koraidon Lv. 72 (Turo: Miraidon Lv. 72) - not part of the listed team. Nemona's final team: only her five fixed members are listed, so levelCap 65 reflects those; her 6th slot is a Lv. 66 starter final evolution that is weak to the player's starter (player Sprigatito -> Quaquaval; Fuecoco -> Meowscarada; Quaxly -> Skeledirge), making her full-team ace level 66. Her Lycanroc is the Midday Form. The False Dragon Titan is one encounter fought as two sequential battles: Dondozo Lv. 56, then Tatsugiri Lv. 57. Team Star bosses end their teams with a Starmobile (a Revavroom variant, recorded via the form field). Atticus fields both a regular Revavroom Lv. 33 and the Navi Starmobile Lv. 32. Ryme's battle is a Double Battle; her Toxtricity is the Low Key Form. Not included in this boss list: the Starfall Street finale battles (Director Clavell Lv. 60-61 and Cassiopeia/Penny Lv. 62-63), Arven's Path of Legends finale battle, and all gym/E4 rematches.",
